# Paths no coding agent may read or write.
#
# Runtime-neutral, gitignore pattern syntax. This file is the ONLY source for the
# Read()/Edit() entries in .claude/settings.json's permissions.deny — regenerate with
# `npm run generate:agent-ignore`, verify with `npm run check:agent-ignore` (CI runs it).
# Editing the settings file by hand will be reverted by the next regeneration.
#
# Scope: secrets only. This is not a "don't look here" list for noisy or large files —
# every entry here is a path whose CONTENTS are credential material.
#
# Two limits worth knowing before you trust this file (see AGENTS.md § Secret paths):
#
# 1. Deny rules cannot carry exceptions. Claude Code evaluates deny before allow and a
#    leading `!` does not exempt anything — verified empirically, not assumed. So the
#    patterns below must never match a placeholder template: `.env.*` is deliberately
#    NOT listed, because it would swallow the tracked, placeholder-only `.env.example`
#    files that onboarding depends on reading. The cost is that a secret-bearing
#    `.env.<name>` outside the forms below is not covered here — .gitignore still stops
#    it being committed, but an agent could read it.
#
# 2. Enforcement is per-runtime. Claude Code enforces this file (generated into
#    permissions.deny). No other agent runtime reads it today. For those, it is a
#    declaration, not a control.

# Local environment files holding resolved secret values.
# `.env.example` templates are intentionally NOT matched — they are placeholder-only,
# tracked, and required reading for onboarding.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Key material — GitHub App private keys, TLS material, signing keys.
*.pem
*.key

# infra/ scratch files. .gitignore allowlists this directory rather than denylisting it
# because secret-bearing scratch files here have repeatedly been named things no pattern
# catches (a stray "New Text Document.txt" is present as of 2026-08-05). infra/ holds no
# legitimate .txt, so denying the extension outright costs nothing.
infra/*.txt
